Mplus VERSION 9.1 (Mac)
MUTHEN & MUTHEN
11/15/2026   9:30 PM

INPUT INSTRUCTIONS

  TITLE:
  2-Level EMA MSEM: Latent Random Slopes Predicting Burnout;
  VARIABLE:
  CLUSTER = id;
  USEVARIABLES = exhaust burnout na1-na3 st1-st3;
  WITHIN = na1-na3 st1-st3;
  BETWEEN = burnout;
  NAMES = exhaust burnout na1 na2 na3 st1 st2 st3 id;
  MISSING = .;
  ANALYSIS:
  TYPE = TWOLEVEL RANDOM;
  ESTIMATOR = BAYES;
  CHAINS = 2;
  PROCESSORS = 4;
  BITERATIONS = 6000 (2500);
  BSEED = 2026;
  MODEL:
  %WITHIN%
  eta_na BY na1@1 na2 na3;
  eta_st BY st1@1 st2 st3;
  s_na | exhaust ON eta_na;
  s_st | exhaust ON eta_st;
  %BETWEEN%
  exhaust s_na s_st;
  exhaust s_na s_st WITH exhaust s_na s_st;
  burnout ON exhaust (b_int)
  s_na (b_sna)
  s_st (b_sst);
  SAVEDATA:
  FILE = ema_fscores.dat;
  SAVE = FSCORES (50 10);
  OUTPUT:
  TECH8;
  DATA:
  FILE = "ema_msem.dat";



*** WARNING in MODEL command
  In the MODEL command, the following variable is an x-variable on the BETWEEN
  level and a y-variable on the WITHIN level.  This variable will be treated
  as a y-variable on both levels:  EXHAUST
